CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* real to complex: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* std::complex: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
dropped the body
--
GNU extension: a real value converts to a complex type.  `z = 4.0' was
rejected, which in a system header dropped the body of
std::complex<double>::operator=(double), so the assignment did nothing.
